1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,901
Jen is fifty-three.

2
00:00:01,961 --> 00:00:04,169
Today she starts GLP-1 therapy.

3
00:00:04,229 --> 00:00:07,609
On paper, everything is in place — a prescription,

4
00:00:07,669 --> 00:00:10,430
a plan, and a follow-up in twelve weeks.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:13,695
But therapy isn’t won or lost in the clinic.

6
00:00:13,755 --> 00:00:17,330
It’s won or lost in the ten weeks nobody is watching.

7
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:20,038
A copay higher than she expected.

8
00:00:20,098 --> 00:00:23,530
A side effect she doesn’t want to make a fuss about.

9
00:00:23,590 --> 00:00:26,150
A refill she keeps meaning to pick up.

10
00:00:26,510 --> 00:00:29,083
None of it reaches her care team.

11
00:00:29,143 --> 00:00:29,690
Not yet.

12
00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:36,168
Preventra reads the signals already in her utilization data — and helps

13
00:00:36,228 --> 00:00:41,318
identify patients who may be at elevated risk of discontinuing therapy.

14
00:00:41,378 --> 00:00:43,810
Weeks before the next appointment.

15
00:00:44,170 --> 00:00:46,104
It doesn’t stop at the flag.

16
00:00:46,164 --> 00:00:52,267
It surfaces the likely drivers behind it — cost pressure, a disrupted appointment,

17
00:00:52,327 --> 00:00:58,730
friction with side effects — so the team knows what to address, not just who to call.

18
00:00:59,090 --> 00:01:03,636
So the conversation happens now, while there’s still time to act.

19
00:01:03,696 --> 00:01:07,710
The decision stays where it belongs — with Jen’s care team.

20
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:10,467
And the same intelligence scales.

21
00:01:10,527 --> 00:01:17,183
Across a population, Preventra gives providers and payers visibility into adherence patterns,

22
00:01:17,243 --> 00:01:24,910
intervention priority, and downstream cost exposure — so attention reaches the patients who need it first.

23
00:01:25,370 --> 00:01:27,332
Preventra GLP-1 Intelligence.

24
00:01:27,392 --> 00:01:30,730
From GLP-1 utilization to treatment intelligence.
